Bound message tubes, sealed correspondence boxes, and orderly shelves
fill this compact dispatch office. The Keeper of Dispatch handles staff
mail with the same seriousness given to any other record of duty. The
room is intentionally mundane: reliable communication is part of
maintaining the world, not a magical privilege to be taken for granted.
The northern complex lies west.
~
