#1291
@WThe @CBu@Bil@Wde@Cr's @BBri@Wef@Cin@Wg @CRo@Bom@n~
Maps, reset diagrams, sample room plans, and blank design slates cover
the walls of this briefing room. The Builder Academy remains the proper
place to learn OLC fundamentals, but this chamber explains the staff
expectation behind those tools: inspect existing content, work inside
assigned authority, preserve cross-zone dependencies, test changes, and
use explicit staging when committing world data. Builders who need a
refresher should visit the Builder Academy rather than experimenting
blindly in a live area.
~
