#1293
@WThe @BHa@Cll @Wof @RJu@Wst@Bic@Ce @Wand @RCo@Wnd@Buc@Ct@n~
Pale marble columns support a solemn hall used for staff conduct reviews
and difficult administrative decisions. Reliefs along the walls depict
scales, an open hand, a guarded gate, and a shield turned outward in
defense of the realm. The symbolism is intentionally civic rather than
divine. Immortals who act here are expected to document what happened,
separate evidence from assumption, use the least authority necessary,
and remember that trust in the staff is part of the world they are
responsible for protecting.
~
